**what happened**

- www.example.com. A is 93.184.216.34, answered by a.iana-servers.net. for example.com.
- a cache may hold this answer for 1 hour, and the delegation to example.com. for 2 days
- 198.51.100.53 is answering this from its cache, with 1 minute left on the copy it is serving
- the chain of trust holds from the root to example.com., signed with ECDSAP256SHA256
- ⚠ 1 server did not answer in time: b.gtld-servers.net.
- ⚠ 1 server answered with almost nothing left of the datagram the answer had to fit in (a.iana-servers.net. with 1187 of 1232 bytes), so one more record in the zone truncates it, and every resolver that asks then pays a second round trip over TCP for the whole of it
